[h1]Smart Notifications Mod for Victoria 3 [/h1]
[b]Less notification noise, a watchlist for the countries you actually care about, and new alerts vanilla is missing.[/b]

Vanilla drowns you in notifications about random countries. This mod retunes what pops up, lets you flag the countries you actually care about, and adds a few alerts the base game should have had.


[h1]Key Features[/h1]

[b]Country watchlist[/b] just like EU IV
[list]
[*] Flag any country in the world (smart defaults: great powers, neighbors, rivals).
[*] Diplomatic plays, wars, and countries joining a side only pop up when a watchlisted country (or you) is actually involved.
[*] Everything else goes to the feed instead of interrupting you.
[/list]

[b]Retuned notification defaults[/b]
[list]
[*] Low-value vanilla notifications demoted from popup/toast to feed or mute.
[/list]

[b]New alerts[/b]
[list]
[*] [b]Truce expired[/b]: get a toast when a truce you had with a country expired.
[*] [b]Taxation Deficit[/b]: alert plus a one-time toast naming the specific state with a taxation capacity deficit
[*] [b]Agitator Invite Available[/b]: fires when you have an open agitator slot and an exiled character eligible to fill it.
[*] [b]Law Ready to Enact[/b]: flag a law you're working toward from its detail panel; get an alert plus a one-time toast the moment it has better odds of passing than stalling.
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]Already played Victoria 3 before?[/h1]

[b]Open Message Settings (the bell icon) and press "Reset to Default Settings" once.[/b] Victoria 3 remembers every notification setting you have ever changed by hand, and those saved choices override any mod. Without that one reset, parts of this mod will silently do nothing. A fresh install needs no reset.

[hr][/hr]

[h1]Compatibility[/h1]

[list]
[*] [b]Game version:[/b] 1.13.* (current patch)
[*] [b]Save games:[/b] safe to add or remove mid-campaign. Note that removing the mod does not restore vanilla notification behaviour on its own — the game keeps the settings as the mod left them until you press "Reset to Default Settings".
[*] [b]Achievements:[/b] unaffected
[*] [b]Multiplayer:[/b] single-player only
[*] [b]File overrides:[/b] this mod fully overrides three vanilla files — [i]common/messages/00_messages.txt[/i] (the notification retuning), [i]gui/message_settings.gui[/i] (the Watchlist tab) and [i]gui/politics_panel_change_law.gui[/i] (flagging a law from its detail panel). Everything else it adds sits in its own files: [i]common/alert_types/[/i], [i]common/alert_groups/[/i] and its own message and localization files are additive, with no vanilla file touched.
[/list]

[b]Known conflicts:[/b] any other mod that fully overrides one of those same three files. Whichever loads later in your playset wins for that entire file — they do not merge. In practice that means another notification-tuning mod (for [i]00_messages.txt[/i]) or a UI overhaul that reworks the message settings or politics screens (for the two [i].gui[/i] files). If you run one, load order decides which you get. Nothing else known.

[hr][/hr]

[h1]Reporting Issues[/h1]

If something's off, include:
[list]
[*] What you expected vs. what happened.
[*] Your Victoria 3 version and other mods enabled.
[*] Whether you had pressed "Reset to Default Settings" — it explains a surprising number of reports.
[*] A screenshot if it is something you can see.
[/list]

Source and issue tracker: [url=https://github.com/dcoullon/victoria3-smart-notifications]github.com/dcoullon/victoria3-smart-notifications[/url]
